Allowance fallbacks apply only when the preferred{{if .Both}} and alternative routes are{{else}} route is{{end}} under material allowance pressure or exhausted, and only for work the fallback can handle; they never replace a judgment-heavy route.{{if .Codex}} Luna is also the default for Codex worker subagents on mechanical or extraction tasks.{{end}}

**Shape test.** Micro requires an explicit outcome, tiny named surface, no discovery and a direct checker. Bounded requires a small familiar surface, close specification, reversibility and strong acceptance criteria. Standard begins with meaningful exploration, cross-file coupling, debugging, non-trivial design or a weak success signal. Deep is ambiguous long-horizon work, security architecture, difficult concurrency or consequential migration design.

Do not restart a stage merely because its shape rises. Continue safe inspection, then reroute the next owner/run when the current route lacks enough capability. A cheaper attempt that produces usable evidence is not wasted; include that evidence in the reroute. After one failure, do not repeat the materially identical attempt.

Exposure controls action gates, not model intelligence. A Consequential but tiny action may be Micro yet still needs its boundary check; a difficult Local refactor may be Deep without requiring permission. Consult targets: {{.AdvisorList}}; use the consult skill. Fix follows Implement; Plan Next follows Plan.

## Plan allowance

These routes were generated from the plan you declared; agentfile never inspects accounts or queries live usage. A declared plan is a routing hint, not proof that a model is enabled in the account.

